# `@ai-agent/client` (client-sdk) purpose

`client-sdk` (`@ai-agent/client`) is the **typed HTTP/SSE client for headless callers** that need to talk to the Baize AI agent backend directly — scripts, integrations, IDE bridges, automation, other services — **not** the main browser UI stack.

## Do

- Extend / stabilize the SDK for programmatic chat, skills, agents, auth (JWT), and SSE streaming.
- Keep wire types aligned with the protocol / server API.
- Point external consumers (Node, Bun, edge, integrations) at this package.

## Don't

- Add `@ai-agent/client` as a dependency of `client/web`.
- Treat `client-sdk` as the data layer for the React SPA.
- Force the SPA to replace `agentApi` / `_http` SSO auth with `AgentClient`.
- Pull Node-only helpers (e.g. `mintJwt` / `node:crypto`) into the browser bundle.

## Web UI

Session/chat HTTP stays on `client/web/src/lib/api/*`. SSE parsing for the SPA lives in `client/web/src/lib/sse.js` (mirrors SDK `parseSSE` — keep wire shape in sync if either changes).
